# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Split Pane, end to end: the document shown twice, one pane above the
# other with a bar between them; what is typed in one pane shows in both,
# and only the pane with the keys draws its caret.  Every pixel below is
# checked against what the same place showed before the step it proves:
# the bar's own pixel, glyph pixels of the same letters in each pane, and
# a caret column in each pane.
wait 14
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
key H
wait 3
key I
wait 6
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-split-one.png
note one pane: the bar's place and the lower half are the page's ground
expect-pixel 500 313 ffffff
expect-pixel 245 325 ffffff
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Split Pane
menu-pick Split Pane
wait 20
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-split-two.png
note split: the bar across the page, the text again in the lower pane,
note and the caret drawn in the upper pane only, which keeps the keys
expect-pixel 500 313 d8d8d8
expect-pixel 245 325 232323
expect-pixel 260 150 000000
expect-pixel 260 328 ffffff
note a press in the lower pane gives it the keys; what it types shows in
note both panes, and now only the lower pane draws its caret
click 300 400
wait 6
key X
wait 12
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-split-typed.png
expect-pixel 264 326 1a1a1a
expect-pixel 264 148 1a1a1a
expect-pixel 268 328 000000
expect-pixel 260 150 ffffff
click 212 8
wait 6
expect-menu Split Pane
menu-pick Split Pane
wait 20
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-split-back.png
note one pane again: the bar is gone and the text stays
expect-pixel 500 313 ffffff
expect-pixel 264 148 1a1a1a
note put the editor away: it asks about the unsaved text, and Discard
note closes it
click-window Edit
wait 6
key Escape
wait 8
click 592 318
wait 60
expect-no-title Edit
quit
